 ],
 "literal": "Greatness having attained, those who are excellent, their firmness in action, with the king, impact having attained, will be esteemed.",
 "translation": "The firmness in action of those who have attained greatness and excellence will reach the ruler, yield successful results, and be highly esteemed.",
 "modern": "பெருமை பெற்றுச் சிறந்தவர்களுடைய செயல் உறுதியானது, அரசனிடத்துச் சென்று பயனைத் தந்து, எல்லாராலும் மதிக்கப்படும்.",
 "explanation": "This couplet explains how unwavering determination in action is recognized and valued. When individuals of noble character and excellence (maṇṭār) possess firmness in action (vinaittiṭpam), their resolve does not go unnoticed. It reaches the attention of the ruler (vēntankaṇ) and produces tangible, successful results (ūṟu). Consequently, their strength of purpose is highly praised and esteemed (uḷḷappaṭum) by the sovereign and society alike.",
